 # Assistant panel
 
+## Vibe Engineer panel
+
+Open a drawing, then choose **View ▸ Palettes ▸ Assistant** or run `ASSISTANT`.
+The panel opens on the right at 380 px and can be resized, collapsed, and
+closed. It connects only to a service on loopback (`127.0.0.1`). Conversation,
+Sources, and Change Plan remain separate sections. After a supported query,
+Sources displays the service-reported session/document/revision, drawing path,
+and available element handles or fact paths, alongside the current selection
+count.
+
+The current local service is read-only. With no OpenRouter key, `/summary`,
+`/entity HANDLE`, and `/help` still work; model questions return a no-key
+message without a provider request. The panel enables Send only after the
+service reports a connected CAD bridge. The service has no mutating CAD tools,
+so it cannot edit the drawing. Structural assessment is also disabled.
+
 `ASSISTANT` (alias `AI`, or **View ▸ Palettes ▸ Assistant**) opens a dockable
 chat pallet for an AI agent that drives the open drawing. The pallet is only
 the user interface: the agent itself is an external service running on the
